"""A Level Economics (0725), Upper Sixth: practice sets for Macroeconomic Problems, International Economics, Economic Growth,
Development & the Cameroonian Economy, and the Examination module.

One 8-question set per lesson (14 topic lessons, 3 examination lessons), plus 'Paper 1 mock exam A' (50 multiple-choice
questions across all six Upper Sixth modules in proportion to their topic counts), 'Paper 2 practice paper A' and
'Paper 3 practice paper A' (auto-markable parts in numbered questions). Exam facts are only those of the Board's 2023 subject
report (Paper 1 = 50 multiple-choice questions, 30%; Paper 2 = 8 essays in micro and macro sections, answer five with not more
than three from a section, 40%; Paper 3 = 5 application questions, answer three, 30%). The timings of the mock papers (90 and
150 minutes) are KKEVO practice settings. All country data are invented for practice. Every numerical answer was checked by
script.
"""

